                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Introduction"><p align="justify">School of Health Sciences (SOHS) was established in 1987. Since that time 2 disciplines i.e. ‘Nursing’ and ‘Health Sciences’ are approved to promote various programmes to strengthen the knowledge and update skills of health professionals and various categories of health care workers. SOHS has designed and developed various programmes in the areas of Medicine, Surgery, Nursing, Dentistry, Allied Health Sciences, AYUSH etc. in collaboration with professional councils, ministries, government and non-governmental organzations of national and international repute. The programme package consist of customized and self directed learning materials, supplementary/complementary audio-videos, teleconferencing and radio conferencing. Practical component is an integral part of all programmes and at least 50% of the learning time is earmarked for the same. The students are attached to identified learner support centres established in reputed tertiary or secondary level health institutions like medical/nursing/dental colleges/district hospitals for skills training under the guidance and supervision of experienced acadmic counsellors (trainers). The students are further attached to Skill Development Centres established in secondary level hospitals or at their own health institutions for practicing skills for competency proficiency and learning to work in resource constrained environment. Indian Nursing Council has given credit hours for few nursing diploma and certificate programs to offer as Continuing Nursing Education programs, this will help in-service nurses to add credits/hours for renewing the registration as RNRM with various state councils. SOHS also launched skill program Qualification Pack - Nurse Manager approved by NSQC. Swayam program on Life Style Diseases is also offered by SOHS.</p align="justify"></div>

                                        
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Objectives"  ><p>School of Health Sciences was established in 1991 with the  objectives:
<ul><li>Plan, Develop and launch doctoral, degree, diploma and certificate level programme for various categories of health professionals including in-service doctors and nurses.
</li><li>Plan, develop and offer health awareness courses for general public
</li><li>Conduct research on health issues</li></ul></p></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-3" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="History"  ><p align="justify"><ul>
<li>In 1987 School of Health Sciences was established after approval in BOM.</li>
<li>In 1990 Planning Board had recommended the launching of a 2-year Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing Degree Programme as proposed by the Indian Nursing Council. Academic Council approved the proposal and authorised the Vice-Chancellor to initiate necessary steps to finalise the programme after due consultation with the Indian Nursing Council. In 1991, 5th AC Academic Council approved the content and structure of the proposed programme in Nursing.</li>
<li>In 1991, in 6th AC, Nursing and Health Sciences disciplines were assigned.</li>
<li>In 1992, 7th AC, The School Board of the School of Health Sciences at its meeting held on 7.9.92 finalised the course structure of the BSc (Nursing) Programme after taking into account the observations made by the Academic Council. The School Board also finalised the practical component of the programme. It was pointed out that in view of the urgency, the Vice Chancellor had approved the course content and the practical component of the BSc (Nursing).</li>
<li>Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing program was the first programme to be offered by SOHS, launched in 1994 for in-service nurses on the request of Indian Nursing Council (INC). It was flagship professional programme delivered through ODL mode in the country. Programme Study centres are established in the Colleges inspected and approved by INC. Admission of candidates is through Common Entrance Examination aimed at merit based selection by region-wise Counselling. The programme has been revised twice i.e. 1st year 2005-07 & 2nd revision in 2021 to 2023. Integration with CCH programme is also done and implemented from year 2023 of first year.</li>
<li>In 1995, in 13thAC, approved Diploma in Maternal and Child Health for Medical Officers.</li>
<li>In 1995, in 13th AC, approved course structure for certificate in Geriatric Medicine.</li>
<li>In 1997, 16th AC, implementation strategy of PGDMCH was approved.</li>
<li>The implementation of Post Graduate Diploma in Maternal & Child Health Programme (PGDMCH) in 1997 was a pioneering effort by IGNOU that created an implementation model of imparting clinical training through blended learning. It also integrated the training process in Paediatrics, Obstetrics & Gynaecology and Community Medicine which are the corner stone for providing primary health care. The programme has been revised in 2003, 2008 and 2018.</li>
<li>Diplomat of National Board recognized and allowed learners of IGNOU completing one year Post Graduate Diploma in Maternal & Child Health (PGDMCH) & Post Graduate Diploma in Hospital & Health Management (PGDHHM) to provide lateral entry for its relevant courses.</li>
<li>In 1998, 18th AC, Phase 3 form of Rural Surgery was approved. To multi-skill the surgeons working in rural areas, IGNOU launched Certificate Programme in Rural Surgery (CRS) in 2001.</li>
<li>In 2000, 23rd AC, change in the code of B.Sc. (Nursing) be to Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing programme.</li>
<li>In 2000, 24th AC, phase 3 form of Diploma in Geriatric Medicine was approved.</li>
<li>In 2000, 24th AC implementation of Certificate in Rural Surgery programme was approved.</li>
<li>In 2000, 24th AC, phase 3 of PGDHHM was approved.</li>
<li>Post Graduate Diploma in Hospital and Health Management was launched in 2001.</li>
<li>IGNOU pioneered in training about a hundred of medical college faculty in IMNCI in 2003 when national level training was being planned by Health Ministry. Similarly, IGNOU trained about a hundred of medical faculty in adolescent health in 2007 in collaboration with World Health Organisation (WHO) when it was yet to be taken up by Health Ministry, Government of India.</li>
<li>IGNOU provided competency in Geriatric Medicine through open and distance learning mode in the year 2004 when there was no precedence of training large number of MBBS doctors in this area. The programme has been revised and revised programme is on offer since January, 2022.</li>
<li>To improve the provision of Cardiac Care in small towns & taluka level hospitals about 1700 M.B.B.S Doctors have been trained in Clinical Cardiology between 2006 to 2016.</li>
<li>Diploma in Nursing Administration was launched in 2006-2025 for in-service nurse to update their managerial skills and considered as CNE by Indian nursing Council.</li>
<li>SOHS in collaboration with Dental Council of India (DCI) initiated innovative PG specialization in Oral Implantology (PGCOI) and endodontic in 2008.</li>
<li>SOHS has played a pioneering role in launching Ph.D. (Nursing) in 2009 till 2022. Executive Committee of the Indian Nursing Council held on 24th December, 2024, resolved that the PhD Nursing by IGNOU shall be recognized qualification for the purpose of the said Act namely: - Ph.D. in Nursing qualification granted by the Indira Gandhi National Open University, Central University, Maidan Garhi, New Delhi. ́</li>
<li>IGNOU created a precedence at national level by designing and implementing an online programme of Post Graduate Diploma in Bio-ethics (PGDBE) Programme in collaboration with Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR) in 2011.</li>
<li>Diploma in Critical Care Nursing was launched in 2011 and considered as CNE by Indian Nursing Council.</li>
<li>To meet the training man power need for Medical Officers of ART centre, IGNOU in collaboration with NACO developed and launched the Post Graduate Diploma in HIV Medicine (PGDHIVM) in 2011.</li>
<li>To meet the training man power need for start along dialysis unit across the Country, IGNOU in collaboration with DGHS, pioneered in starting a Post Doctoral Certificate in Dialysis Medicine (PDCDM) in 2011.</li>
<li>Certificate in Community Health (CCH) programme developed in collaboration with Ministry of H&FW, GOI, was launched in 2017 with the objective to provide comprehensive primary health care at Grass Roots level by trained manpower as CHOs. IGNOU is contributing towards strengthening of health care as envisaged in Ayushman Bharat under NHM. Candidates are sponsored through states NHM and ensure 100% placement of the successful candidates at Health & Wellness centres. Awarded Best Certificate programme in 36th IGNOU Foundation Day on 19th November 2021. More than 40,857 students have enrolled in programme till July, 2025.</li>
<li>To scale up the implementation of biomedical waste management rules (2016) across the Country, Ministry has identified IGNOU to train the nodal officers & quality assurance officers of all States, through its Certificate in Health Care Waste Management (CHCWM) Programme. State of Delhi, Gujarat, Odisha have also sponsored their candidates for the programme. WHO Maldives also invited IGNOU to train its Masters trainers in Health Care Waste Management and supervised the cascade training in the Atolls in 2024. The programme was awarded the Best Certificate Programme in 38th IGNOU Foundation on 19th November, 2023.</li>
<li>To create national preparedness for medical management of CBRNE disaster, IGNOU pioneered in designing the (PGCMDM) programme in collaboration with INMAS, DRDO in 2019. DGAFMS, CAPF, NDRF, BSF, ESIC Reliance, DGHS, and Hospital under DGHS sponsored candidates for this programme.</li>
<li>Subsequently various certificate programmes were developed and are being offered to in-service nurses Certificate in Newborn & Infant Nursing, Certificate in Maternal and Child Health Nursing as CNE by Indian nursing Council. Few certificate programmes have also been developed for the general public,.i.e. Certificate Diabetes Care Worker, Certificate in in Home Based Health Care, Certificate in First Aid programme and Certificate Programme in Yoga (CPY). Certificate in Adolescent Health and counselling was re-launched in 2021 for school teachers and graduates School of Health Sciences has also contributed by developing training material for Patient Safety & Infection Control for DGHS. 4 skill programmes were launched through MoU with MOH&FW, GOI since 2019 but 2 programmes are only on offer till 2025.</li>
<li>In 2025 Qualification Pack – Nurse Manager (QPNM) as per NCVET guidelines and approved by NSQC on 22-10-204 was launched in July 2025 for in-service Nurses to update their management knowledge and skills. QPNM approved by Indian Nursing Council as Continuing Nursing Education and given 55 hours/11 credits on 31-12-2025.</li>
<li>Executive Emergency Healthcare Qualification Pack as per NCVET guidelines and approved by NSQC on 22-10-2024.</li></p align="justify">

</div>
