                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-4" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p align="justify">Welcome Learners to School of Health Sciences (SOHS)<br>
The School of Health Sciences was set up in the year 1987 with the objective of augmenting educational avenues for medical and nursing personnel through distance education mode. School has 2 disciplines Nursing Sciences and Health Sciences. The various functions of the school are planning, designing and developing various programmes at degree, diploma and certificate level for various categories of health professionals; health awareness courses for the general public and conducting research on health issues.<br>
<br>
The school (Nursing Discipline) is pioneer in developing competency-based programmes in nursing i.e. Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing, approved by Indian Nursing Council and various other programmes like Diploma in Critical Care Nursing, Diploma in Nursing Administration, CCH programme for CHO/Midlevel Healthcare Provider and first skill programme to update managerial skills of nurses i.e. Nurse Manager programme approved by INC as CNE programme; Health Sciences discipled designed and developed programmes like MBA in Health and Hospital Management, PG Diploma in Maternal and Child Health, Post Graduate Diploma in Health and Hospital Management, Post Graduate Diploma in Geriatric Medicine and various other diploma and certificate programmes for medical graduates. The school adopts an innovative approach in implementing programmes through a diversified approach i.e. three-tier system in medical colleges or nursing colleges as Learner Support Centres (LSCs)], district hospitals as Skill Development Centres and the learners’ work places i.e. hospital for hands on training.<br>
<br>
The school is also collaborating with various National and International organizations i.e. Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Indian Nursing Council, National Medical Commission and reputed organizations like WHO, UNICEF.
Vision of the SOHS is to offer programmes which will benefit the in-service healthcare professionals to update their knowledge and skills and are job ready for future. School also emphasises in building collaborations with various regulatory bodies, industry so that our learners contribute to achieve goals of Sustainable Development Goals to achieve Universal health Coverage, handle any epidemic/pandemic or emergency in future.<br>
Best wishes for your future!<br>
